{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Molecular.ShellCapacitySelfSquare","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Molecular.ShellCapacitySelfSquare","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.shell_capacity_self_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.shell_capacity_self_square","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/ShellCapacitySelfSquare.lean#L46-L56","doc":"**Shell capacity as a self-square.**  Principal shell `n` holds `2n²`\nelectrons: the spin factor `2` times the orbital count\n`n² = ∑_{ℓ<n} (2ℓ+1)`.  Equivalently the bar-even self-square `2[n]_q²`\nevaluated at `q = 1`.  The doubling is the self-fusion of one angular object,\nnot a product of two `SU(2)` factors. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:shell-capacity-self-square","label":"prop:shell-capacity-self-square","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/shell-capacity-self-square.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.orbital_n_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.orbital_n_squared","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Molecular/ShellCapacitySelfSquare.lean#L35-L44","doc":"**Orbital count of principal shell `n` is `n²`.**  The number of orbital\nsub-states in shell `n` is the sum of the sub-shell multiplicities `2ℓ+1`\nover `ℓ = 0, …, n-1` — the sum of the first `n` odd numbers.  This is the\n`q → 1` value of the angular `q`-dimension self-square `[n]_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}